   "response_text": "Found it and squashed it. \ud83d\udc36\n\n**The bug** was in `src/click/parser.py`, in `OptionParser._process_opts` (line 505):\n\n```python\nlong_opt, explicit_value = arg.split(\"=\")[:2]\n```\n\n`arg.split(\"=\")` on `--name=a=b=c` gives `['--name', 'a', 'b', 'c']`, and `[:2]` keeps only `['--name', 'a']` \u2014 silently throwing away `=b=c`. So the option name parsed fine but the value got truncated at the second `=`.\n\n**The fix** \u2014 split only on the *first* equals, exactly what `.partition()` is for:\n\n```python\nlong_opt, _, explicit_value = arg.partition(\"=\")\n```\n\nNow everything after the first `=` becomes the value. Verified:\n- `--name=a=b=c` \u2192 `'a=b=c'` \u2705\n- `--name=a` \u2192 `'a'` \u2705\n- `--name=a=` \u2192 `'a='` \u2705\n\nFull test suite: **588 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed** \u2014 no regressions. Only the one library source file was touched; no tests were added, edited, or deleted.\n\nDONE",
